<metadata><name>Rosary Lakes</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:290-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.601292" lon="-122.036453"><ele>1565.4</ele><name>Willamette Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM node 2630339680, Willamette Pass Resort lot); confidence: high; pdf_page: 292; book_elev_ft: 5128; quote: map 65: WILLAMETTE PASS 5128'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.597173" lon="-122.033710"><ele>1553.6</ele><name>PCT trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM: junction of PCT Section D and E ways, by the PCT parking east of the highway (as in 291-1); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 292; quote: follows the PCT 3 miles from Willamette Pass, starting behind the Department of Highways shed just east of the lodge area</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.604112" lon="-121.996913"><ele>1748.6</ele><name>Lower Rosary Lake, north end</name><desc>source: PCT by the north end of Lower Rosary Lake (OSM lake way 189154487), where map 65's 3.0 mi leg ends; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 292; book_elev_ft: 5707; quote: Lower Rosary Lake, also known as South Rosary or Ethel, is at 5,707 feet, a 580-foot climb from the trailhead.</desc></wpt>
